		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://drownedmadonna.com/?p=1420</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[<p>Many artists have helped raise awareness of LGBT issues through their work, but only one artist has made the top [...]</p>
<p>The post <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com/madonna-1-artist-helped-lgbt-movement/20140721">Madonna is the #1 artist who has helped the LGBT movement.</a> appeared first on <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com">Madonna new album news unapologetic</a>.</p>
]]></description>
				<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><span style="color: #555555;">Many artists have helped raise awareness of <strong>LGBT</strong> issues through their work, but only one artist has made the top spot, and that&#8217;s <strong>Madonna</strong>, of course.</span></p>
<p>The site <a href="http://lgbteen.org/" target="_blank">LGBTEEN</a> listed the 10 most influential artists who have helped the LGBT cause, here their words about the Queen of Pop:</p>
<blockquote class="pixcode  pixcode--testimonial  testimonial testimonial--small-text">
    <div class="testimonial__content">
<p>In the 1980s, many people were using the AIDS epidemic as an excuse to perpetuate homophobia. Madonna was one of the first mainstream figures who spoke out in defense of the gay community at this time. She got involved in the fight against AIDS, encouraging research and the practice of safe sex. She brought vogueing—a style of dance started in New York’s gay club scene—to the mainstream and featured footage from a gay pride parade in her tour documentary, “Truth or Dare.” She also featured gay, lesbian, and bisexual affection in “Truth or Dare,” the “Justify My Love” video and her “Sex” book. This was still in the early 1990s, before it was a trendy thing for female pop stars to do. More recently, Madonna has spoken out against bullying, anti-gay laws in Malawi and Russia, and the Boy Scouts’ anti-gay policy. Madonna’s advocacy for the LGBT community was acknowledged when gay news magazine, “The Advocate,” named Madonna “the greatest gay icon” in 2012.</p>
</div>

    </blockquote>

<p><strong>She has risked her own populatiry to stand by what she believes in. And that&#8217;s what makes Madonna so admirable, </strong>they added.</p>
<p>The other artists who have made the top 10 are:</p>
<ul>
<li>Janet Jackson</li>
<li>Macklemore &amp; Lewis</li>
<li>Demi Lovato</li>
<li>Melissa Etheridge</li>
<li>Christina Aguilera</li>
<li>Pansy Division</li>
<li>Mika</li>
<li>Kurt Cobain</li>
<li>Johnny Dangerous</li>
</ul>
<h2 style="color: #555555;"></h2>
<p>The post <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com/madonna-1-artist-helped-lgbt-movement/20140721">Madonna is the #1 artist who has helped the LGBT movement.</a> appeared first on <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com">Madonna new album news unapologetic</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
